Operator 2026-06-21: 'This has happened multiple times now. How do we capture the ask so we
aren't constantly re-learning that we are working on a live agent ... an agent local loop that
can discover how to solve hidden games given to it at challenge submission time?'

The project's anti-re-learning mechanism is a MANDATORY CLAUDE.md rule -- the one artifact the
planner + every agent read as required input each session (memory is unreachable from the planner
subprocess). Added 'ARC-AGI-3 IS a Live Hidden-Game Discovery Agent -- Foundational Framing
(MANDATORY)' + Rule Index entry + ops/north-star.md §0 reinforcement + the
feedback_arc_value_is_process_not_weights memory. The rule states the settled framing (live runtime
discovery loop over unseen games: induce perception+dynamics+goal at runtime) and the three
recurring errors it kills: (1) trained weights are not the live mechanism, (2) public-game
replays are not the scored deliverable, (3) an offline null may be a corpus/harness artifact --
verify before concluding (this session's n_win_states=0 / corpus lb=la=0 trap is the exemplar).

